/-!
# The fibre-difference coefficient of a family of closed subschemes

Rational equivalence of `k`-cycles on `X` over a Chow situation is generated by the
differences `[Z_0]_k - [Z_∞]_k` of the zero and infinity fibres of closed subschemes `Z` of
the family of projective lines `X ×_S ℙ¹_S`. A cycle that is rationally equivalent to zero is
therefore given, coefficient by coefficient, by a locally finite sum of such differences over
a family of closed subschemes (Stacks 02S4, parts (3) and (4)).

This file defines that coefficient function, the coefficientwise sum of the fibre differences of
a family of closed subschemes; for a locally finite family each coefficient is a finite sum.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.familyFibreDifferenceCoefficient` — the coefficient at a point of `X` of the
  total zero-minus-infinity fibre difference of a family of closed subschemes of
  `X ×_S ℙ¹_S`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02S4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02S4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-- The coefficient at `x : X` of the sum over `j` of the zero fibre cycle minus the infinity
fibre cycle of a family `W` of closed subschemes of `X ×_S ℙ¹_S`. The sum is a `finsum`: it
is the finite sum of the nonzero terms when only finitely many are nonzero, as happens at
every `x` for a locally finite family, and is zero when infinitely many are. -/
def familyFibreDifferenceCoefficient (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (k : ℤ)
    {J : Type u} (W : J → (projectiveLineProduct f).IdealSheafData) (x : X) : ℤ :=
  ∑ᶠ j : J,
    ((cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (zeroFiber f (W j)).subschemeι k).1 x -
      (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (infinityFiber f (W j)).subschemeι k).1 x)

end Stacks.Chow

end
